An attempt at an advisory patch. As Pasi notes, getobj() is a horrible
place; this method is kludgy, but I don't think it's any kludgier than
some of the stuff that's already there. GOLDOBJ is the main problem,
but I've tested this briefly with and without that, and it _seems_ to
work either way...

